{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, בְּהַל","hw":"בְּהַל","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">בְּהַל</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. </strong><br><strong>Pa.</strong>  <strong> alarm, dismay (</strong>so usually 𝔗 (not Syriac); BH <span dir=\"rtl\">[בָּהַל]</span><strong>)</strong>;—Impf. 3 ms. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבַהֲלָךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:16\" href=\"/Daniel.4.16\">Dn 4:16</a> and 3 mpl. sf. -<span dir=\"rtl\">לֻנַּנִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:2\" href=\"/Daniel.4.2\">4:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:15\" href=\"/Daniel.7.15\">7:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:28\" href=\"/Daniel.7.28\">28</a> (both juss. Str<sup>§ 13 c</sup> M <sup>§ 52 a</sup>); -<span dir=\"rtl\">לוּךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:10\" href=\"/Daniel.5.10\">5:10</a>, -<span dir=\"rtl\">לֻנֵּ֑הּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:16\" href=\"/Daniel.4.16\">4:16</a>, -<span dir=\"rtl\">לוּנֵּהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:6\" href=\"/Daniel.5.6\">5:6</a>.<br><strong>Hithpe.</strong>  <em>hasten</em> <strong>(</strong>so Pi. in late BH; 𝔗 Ithpe. (rare)<strong>)</strong>; Inf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּהִתְבְּהָלָה</span> = <em>in haste</em> (orig. ‘in alarm’) <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:25\" href=\"/Daniel.2.25\">Dn 2:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:24\" href=\"/Daniel.3.24\">3:24</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:20\" href=\"/Daniel.6.20\">6:20</a>.<br><strong>Hithpa.</strong>  Pt. pass. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְבָּהַל</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:9\" href=\"/Daniel.5.9\">Dn 5:9</a> was greatly <em>alarmed</em>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, בְּהִילוּ","prev":"BDB Aramaic, בְּדַר"}